AI presentation makers turn a prompt or an outline into a slide deck. Gamma, Beautiful.ai and Canva are three common choices, and they meter their AI in three different ways: credits, an unlimited-use promise, and monthly usage allowances. That makes the sticker price hard to compare. This guide sets out the published prices and limits as of 12 November 2026, in US dollars.

*Disclosure: this post was drafted by Claude, an AI assistant made by Anthropic, and checked by a separate AI reviewer against the vendor pages. Stackbrook did not test these tools, and has no affiliate relationship with any of them at the time of writing. The header image is AI-generated.*

One note on sources. Prices come from each vendor's own pages. Canva's main pricing page could not be fetched and Gamma's pricing page gave no dollar amounts for its mid tiers, so Canva's price is from its Pro page and its limits from its help center, and Gamma's plan details are from its help center. Where a vendor's pages disagree, this guide says so.

## The prices at a glance

| Plan | Gamma | Beautiful.ai | Canva |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Free | $0, 400 one-time credits | None, 14-day trial | $0, 20 AI uses a month |
| Entry paid, annual billing | Plus, price not found | Pro, $12 or $14.50 | Pro, $119.99 a year (about $10 a month), up to 5 people |
| Entry paid, monthly billing | Plus, price not found | Not listed; a $45 single-presentation option exists (see below) | Pro, $12.99, up to 5 people |
| Team or business, annual billing | Business, $40 per member | Team, $40 per user | Business, price not found |
| Team or business, monthly billing | Not listed | Team, $50 per user | Business, price not found |
| Enterprise | Not listed | Contact sales | Not listed |

Gamma bills paid plans per workspace member, and its help center says annual plans carry a 28% discount on the monthly rate. Beautiful.ai's Pro is a single seat and its Team plan runs from 2 to 20 seats. Canva Pro is the odd one out because its listed price covers up to 5 people rather than one.

![Bar chart of published paid plans on annual billing, in dollars a month: Canva Pro $10, Beautiful.ai Pro $12 or $14.50, Beautiful.ai Team $40, Gamma Business $40](/images/site1/ai-presentation-makers-pricing-compared-chart.svg)
*Chart created by Stackbrook from the vendors' published prices, as cited in this article. Gamma's Plus and Pro prices are missing because we could not find them on a readable vendor page.*

## The free plans

**Gamma.** Its help center says new users get 400 credits at signup and that they do not refresh. Referrals can earn 200 credits each, up to 2,000 at once. AI actions use credits: creating a presentation with AI or its Agent, editing with the Agent, adding cards, trying new layouts and generating images. Manual editing is free. The free plan caps AI generation at up to 10 slides per prompt with basic image models, and the pricing page lists PowerPoint and PDF export among the basic features. Free decks carry the "Made with Gamma" badge, and paid plans remove it, per another help article. Free requires no credit card.

**Beautiful.ai.** There is no permanent free plan. Its pricing page offers a 14-day trial of Pro or Team, requires a credit card, and charges automatically when the trial ends unless you cancel. Students with a valid .edu email can get a year free.

**Canva.** Its help center says the free plan includes up to 20 uses of Standard or Premium AI tools combined, resetting at midnight UTC on the first of each month. Ultra AI tools are not included. At the limit, Standard and Premium tools slow down with short pauses between generations. We did not find a watermark or export policy for the free tier on the pages we could read, so check that before relying on it.

## What the paid plans add

**Gamma** sells Plus, Pro, Ultra and Business tiers, per its help center. Plus gives 1,500 monthly credits that roll over up to 3,000, removes the badge and allows up to 100 slides per prompt. Pro gives 4,000 credits, and Ultra gives 20,000 credits and is monthly billing only. Business is $40 per member a month, billed annually, with 10,000 credits per member, SSO and SOC 2 documentation on request. Gamma's pricing page and its help center disagree: the pricing page describes paid AI creation as unlimited and lists lower card limits than the help center and developer docs do. This guide uses the help center, and you should treat the slide caps as unsettled. Check the live pages for other plan features such as export, domains and analytics. One help article gives a $20 a month plan as a billing example for two users without naming the plan, which is not enough to call it a price for Plus or Pro.

**Beautiful.ai** lists unlimited AI content generation on Pro and Team, with no stated usage caps. Team is aimed at groups of 2 to 20 seats, and the feature lists on its live comparison table are the place to check collaboration, branding and export. The pages disagree in two places. The Pro annual price is $14.50 a month on one page and $12 on another. And one pricing card says Team is $40 a month including 3 users while its FAQ says $40 per user, so confirm with sales before budgeting. A $45 figure also appears on its pages. One describes it as a one-time purchase for a single presentation, and the other lists it with monthly billing, so treat it as unclear.

**Canva** charges $12.99 a month or $119.99 a year for Pro, for up to 5 people, with extra members at $5 a month on the annual plan or $7 on the monthly one. A page in its learning section instead describes Pro as a flat monthly fee for one person, so check the seat terms at checkout. On AI, the help center says Standard tools such as Magic Write do not draw from your allowance on Pro, subject to fair-use limits. Pro adds a shared allowance of up to 200 uses of Premium tools or up to 20 of Ultra tools, and an AI Pass add-on buys more. Business raises that to 400 Premium or 40 Ultra uses per member.

## Which fits which situation

- **You want the lowest published price.** Canva Pro at about $10 a month on annual billing is the lowest price we could verify, and it covers up to 5 people. Beautiful.ai Pro is next at $12 or $14.50. Gamma's cheaper tiers could not be compared.
- **You want to try before paying, with no card.** Gamma and Canva have free plans without a trial card requirement stated on the pages we read, while Beautiful.ai asks for a card for its trial.
- **You make a lot of AI decks.** Gamma and Canva ration AI use, by credits and by monthly uses. Beautiful.ai lists unlimited generation with no stated cap, so read its fair-use terms.
- **You need team controls.** Gamma Business and Beautiful.ai Team are both $40 on annual billing, so compare seat limits, SSO and shared libraries rather than price.

## Before you pay

Run your own prompt through each free plan or trial and check what you can export and whether a badge or watermark appears. Confirm the seat count, because Canva's up-to-5 pricing, Gamma's per-member billing and Beautiful.ai's two Team descriptions each change the real cost for a group. Finally, check the live pricing pages, since two of the three vendors did not give us a clean price through their main page.
